ic spending surge or another round of polls showing Hinojosa ahead would move this to a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Greg Abbott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas Governor Greg Abbott seeks another term against Democratic state representative Gina Hinojosa in a race that has tightened more than expected. Polls through late September show Abbott leading by roughly two to four points, with a few surveys even putting Hinojosa ahead. Abbott holds a commanding financial edge, with about $67 million on hand compared to Hinojosa's $3 million, and he carries the advantages of incumbency in a state that has leaned Republican by about six points.\n\nStill, the closeness of the polling, headlines about a competitive race, and Abbott's own warnings to donors suggest genuine vulnerability. Expert raters mostly call the race Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Hinojosa roughly a one-in-five chance. The race remains competitive but tilts toward Abbott.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1819, "margin": -4.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2894, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2702, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -3.3}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2978, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2717, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2616, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2625, "margin": -3.5}]}